Harbor: a Direct2D effect whose graph holds a node that isn't a draw transform can be created (#93).

Initializing the graph failed the whole effect with E_NOTIMPL for such a node. Office registers effects of its
own whose graphs hold them (an offset transform is enough) and leaves its window blank when one can't be
created. The node is now left without draw info; it takes no part in rendering.

Test: WindowsTests/d2d/run.sh.

--- a/dlls/d2d1/effect.c
+++ b/dlls/d2d1/effect.c
@@ -3528,8 +3528,10 @@
         }
         else
         {
-            FIXME("Unsupported node %p.\n", node);
-            return E_NOTIMPL;
+            /* HARBOR HACK: this failed the whole effect with E_NOTIMPL. Office registers effects of its own
+             * whose graphs hold nodes that aren't draw transforms, and gives up drawing when one can't be
+             * created. Such a node gets no draw info and takes no part in rendering (#93). */
+            FIXME("Node %p is not a draw transform, leaving it out.\n", node);
         }
     }
 
